  "note": "Patcher matrix for B191, BUILT FROM main AT e09a33b (PR #355), seeded from the B190 matrix. Two owner-requested behaviour changes, both confirmed in play on probe builds before this bundle was cut. (1) The spa RECEIVING treatment lasts as long as the GIVING one: both computed GetRandom(11)+55, but PlanToWork counts ticks while PlanToPlayAnim counts animation frames, so the strip was ending early; the strip length is now its own argument and the treatment passes the hammock's confirmed GetRandom(180)+180. (2) The manual hammock drop (behavior 0x24, base and Invisible Hammock alike) is retargeted to a VF2 entry that settles with the NATIVE DROP's own table -- orientation 1 -> PlanToLieDown (body 9) + SleepNW, otherwise PlanToWait(.., 0x17) + SleepNE, no head direction -- then sleeps for GetRandom(180)+180, keeping the native refusal branch and releasing no semaphore; the autonomous route shares the same corrected table. A first probe had shared the autonomous route's inherited mapping (body 9 at both orientations, head split on orientation == 3), which the owner reported as wrong facing plus a flip when the eyes close; native LieInHammock is body 9 + SleepNW unconditionally, a native defect, not a reference. Both changes were decoded from the shipped executable. See docs/B191-release-notes.md, which must not be allowed to disagree with this field.",
